@startuml seq-05-auditoria
title Activity audit - append-only with hash chaining + WORM retention
autonumber

participant "Domain services\n(transfer/payment/identity/...)" as svc
participant "bp-event-bus" as bus
participant "bp-audit-service" as audit
database "bp-db-postgres\n(append-only operational log)" as pg
participant "bp-audit-archive\n(S3 Object Lock WORM)" as worm

== Recording auditable events ==
svc -> bus : publish event (success / failure / auth attempt / rejection / security)
bus -> audit : deliver event (at-least-once)
audit -> audit : Idempotency by eventId (ignore duplicates)
audit -> audit : Minimize PII; compute hash = H(prevHash + payload)
audit -> pg : INSERT append-only (eventId, hash, prevHash, ts)

alt eventId already recorded (bus duplicate)
    pg --> audit : UNIQUE(eventId) conflict
    audit -> audit : Discard (already audited)
else new
    pg --> audit : OK (hash chain extended)
end

== Export to protected retention ==
audit -> worm : Export signed batch to WORM (S3 Object Lock)
note over worm : Immutable by retention policy.\nLOCALLY not simulated (documented only).

== Traceability query ==
actor "Operator/Support" as op
op -> audit : GET /v1/audit?filters
audit -> pg : Query the operational log
audit -> audit : Verify chain integrity (re-hash)
audit --> op : Results + integrity status (OK / BROKEN)
@enduml
